subproblem.statement:
Let n >= 1 and l be natural numbers and p > n real. Let mu be a measure on R^(n+l), H : R^(n+l) -> R^(n+l), w : R^(n+l) -> R, y in R^(n+l), R > 0, Lambda > 0, 0 < eps <= 1, phi : R -> R, and I, E, a : R -> R. Write r_x := |x - y|, phi' := deriv phi and kappa := (p - n)/(4p). Assume:
- mu(B_R(y)) < infinity (closed ball), and H is mu-integrable on B_R(y);
- (ofReal(R^(p-n)) * lower integral over B_R(y) of |H|^p dmu)^(1/p) <= ofReal(kappa Lambda);
- w is a.e.-strongly measurable for mu restricted to ball y R, and 0 <= w(x) <= 1 for mu-a.e. x in ball y R;
- phi is C^1 and nonincreasing, with phi(u) = 1 for u <= 1 and phi(u) = 0 for u >= 1 + eps;
- radial identity: for every rho > 0 with (1+eps) rho < R, integral (n phi(r_x/rho) + (r_x/rho) phi'(r_x/rho)(1 - w(x))) dmu = - integral phi(r_x/rho)(x - y).H(x) dmu;
- for all real t: I(t) = integral phi(r_x/t) dmu, E(t) = integral phi(r_x/t)(x - y).H(x) dmu, and a(t) = E(t)/t^(n+1)/(1 + I(t)/t^n).
Put Phi~(t) := exp(-integral_0^t a)(1 + I(t)/t^n). Then:
(1) for every t > 0 with (1+eps) t < R, a is continuous at t and |a(t)| <= 2 kappa Lambda R^(-1) (t/R)^(-n/p);
(2) for all 0 < s <= r with (1+eps) r < R: Phi~(s) <= Phi~(r), and the lower integral over closedBall y r minus ball y ((1+eps) s) of ofReal(w(x)/|x - y|^n) dmu is at most ofReal(exp(Lambda/2)(Phi~(r) - Phi~(s))).
